 it  impacts the asian plant collections  below  so decisions are made about removals and  thinning and planting  of the overstory but it's largely  in a way or decisions made about the  impact that would have  on the asian plants that grow beneath  and to the best of my knowledge there  haven't been any active studies  up in that canopy  we do engage with researchers from the  university  um but largely  the the research that happens here is  driven by the interests of  of the labs on campus so we provide what  we can based on  what they need as opposed to actively  sort of directing that research so  if if people on campus aren't interested  in studying it we actually don't have  the capacity in our staff  to study it our involvement in research  is to supply material to researchers  as opposed to in-house research  unfortunately we have run out of time  so i want to again thank ben  for an intriguing and information  filled presentation thank you so much  ben  we are sorry that you can't be with us  in person but look forward to seeing you  again sometime in the future  i look forward to visiting thanks don  okay  bye bye now bye  this has been a production of cornell  university  on the web at cornell.edu


